# .env.example for skill `agentmail-send`
# Aggregated into <scope>/skills/agentmail-send/config/.env by
# `make -C skillshub setup-env`. Fill in real values in your
# operator-config.yaml (secrets.*), NOT here.
#
# Multi-account (mirrors the gmail tool's `account` param): each AgentMail
# account is one inbox identity with its OWN inbox-scoped key. The wrapper
# scripts/agentmail-run.sh resolves the selected `account` to its key and maps
# it onto AGENTMAIL_API_KEY (what the agentmail CLI reads).
#
# Default account "work" → magican@agentmail.to uses AGENT_MAIL_KEY:
AGENT_MAIL_KEY=
#
# To add another account <NAME> (alias is flexible), give it its own
# inbox-scoped key + inbox email — add the secrets to operator-config.yaml,
# uncomment the lines below, then re-run `make -C skillshub setup-env`.
# <NAME> is the alias upper-cased with non-alphanumerics -> "_"
# (e.g. account "beta-test" -> BETA_TEST):
#   AGENT_MAIL_KEY_<NAME>=
#   AGENTMAIL_ACCOUNT_<NAME>_EMAIL=
